# Check that the kit-mdc fails in the expected way when given an object file in
# a format for which support has not yet been implemented. This is different
# from binary file formats that can never be supported.
#
# Create temporary working directories
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: rm -rf %t/in && mkdir -p %t/in
#
# Create the object files to be used for testing. The sources are checked in
# to avoid having binary blobs checked in. We need an object file created from
# an empty input file.
#
# RUN: llc --mtriple=x86_64-apple-darwin -filetype=obj %S/input/empty.ll \
# RUN:     -o %t/in/macho.o
#
# RUN: llc --mtriple=x86_64-windows-msvc -filetype=obj %S/input/empty.ll \
# RUN:     -o %t/in/coff.o
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Support for MachO has not been implemented yet, but might become available at
# some point.
#
# RUN: not kit-mdc %t/in/macho.o 2>&1 \
# RUN:     | FileCheck %s -check-prefix MACHO
#
# MACHO: NOT YET IMPLEMENTED: support for object file format 'macho-object'
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It is unlikely that Windows will ever be supported.
#
# RUN: not kit-mdc %t/in/coff.o 2>&1 \
# RUN:     | FileCheck %s -check-prefix COFF
#
# COFF: NOT YET IMPLEMENTED: support for object file format 'coff-object'
